{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2156-07-13 17:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be taking care of you during your stay. Can you tell me what brought you to the hospital?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2156-07-13 17:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi. I’ve had terrible diarrhea for two days—like, nonstop. Then I started vomiting and got this awful belly pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2156-07-13 17:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Was there any fever or blood in the stool?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2156-07-13 17:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I felt feverish, but no blood. The pain started crampy, then got sharp across my upper belly—same as my usual pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2156-07-13 17:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. Given your history of chronic pancreatitis and gastroparesis, this could be a flare-up from a stomach bug. We’ll run some tests."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2156-07-13 17:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been managing okay at home, but this time it just overwhelmed me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2156-07-13 17:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You were given IV fluids and Dilaudid in the ER. We’ll keep you on low-dose pain meds and monitor your blood sugar closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2156-07-13 17:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "My sugars have been low. I got D50 twice already."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2156-07-13 17:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we saw that. Your insulin has been reduced for now since you’re not eating much. We’ll adjust it as you start tolerating feeds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2156-07-13 17:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That makes sense. I’m worried about my G-tube feeds though—sometimes they make me feel worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2156-07-13 17:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll start them slowly. Right now, your belly is tender near the G-tube site, so we’ll wait until nausea improves."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2156-07-14 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your white count is a bit high, which suggests infection, but your liver and pancreas enzymes are stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2156-07-14 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s probably just a virus?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2156-07-14 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Most likely. No signs of bacterial infection so far. We’re holding off antibiotics unless something changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2156-07-14 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m glad. I’ve had bad reactions to penicillin and Bactrim before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2156-07-14 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve noted your allergies. No antibiotics planned unless absolutely necessary."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2156-07-15 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your nausea is better today. We’d like to restart your tube feeds at a low rate and see how you tolerate it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2156-07-15 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, but go slow. I don’t want to start vomiting again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2156-07-15 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll start at 20 cc/hr and increase only if you’re comfortable. A nurse will monitor you closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2156-07-15 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Feeds are running at 20 cc/hr. You’re doing well so far."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2156-07-15 12:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel okay. Not nauseous."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2156-07-16 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great news—you’re up to 40 cc/hr and keeping it down. We’re going to increase to 50 later today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2156-07-16 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. My belly pain is also less intense now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2156-07-16 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve been giving low-dose IV Dilaudid, but you’re needing it less. We’ll switch to oral pain meds soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2156-07-16 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I usually take tramadol at home. Can I go back on that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2156-07-16 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We offered it yesterday, but you declined. If you’re comfortable, we can restart it, but your team recommends tapering off."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2156-07-16 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I didn’t want it then—I felt groggy. But I’ll take it if the pain comes back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2156-07-17 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your stool tests came back negative for C. diff, Salmonella, Shigella, and Campylobacter. That supports a viral cause."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2156-07-17 08:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it wasn’t food poisoning?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2156-07-17 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Unlikely. No bacterial pathogens were found. Your body is clearing it on its own."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2156-07-17 08:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I was worried I did something wrong."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2156-07-17 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not at all. Viruses happen. Your chronic conditions just make recovery slower."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2156-07-18 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve been off IV pain meds since yesterday. How’s the pain today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2156-07-18 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Much better. Just mild discomfort now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2156-07-18 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "And your blood sugars are stabilizing. We’re increasing your insulin back toward your home doses."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2156-07-18 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m glad. I don’t want my diabetes to get worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2156-07-18 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re following your usual regimen. You’re on glargine at night and U-500 regular insulin with feeds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2156-07-19 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Psychiatry checked in. They say your mood and anxiety are stable on Seroquel, Valium, and trazodone."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2156-07-19 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been sleeping better. Still anxious, but manageable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2156-07-19 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "They recommend continuing your meds. There’s a referral out for long-term support, but no response yet."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2156-07-19 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’d like more help, but it’s hard to find someone who takes my insurance."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2156-07-19 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re trying to connect you with a provider. In the meantime, your current plan is working."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2156-07-20 09:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve been at 50 cc/hr for tube feeds for two days with no issues. That’s your goal rate."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2156-07-20 09:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel stronger. Can I go home soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2156-07-20 09:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly by tomorrow. We’ll make sure your pain is controlled and you’re stable on insulin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2156-07-20 09:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I don’t want to leave if I’m not ready."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2156-07-20 09:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We won’t discharge you unless you’re safe. You’ll go home with hydromorphone for breakthrough pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2156-07-20 09:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Not tramadol?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2156-07-20 09:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You refused it multiple times here, so we’re discontinuing it. Your primary doctor will help you taper if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2156-07-20 09:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that’s fine. I’d rather not take it if I don’t have to."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2156-07-21 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Final plan: You’ll go home tomorrow. We’ll send you with instructions for insulin, feeds, and pain meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2156-07-21 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about my asthma? I’ve been using my inhaler more."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2156-07-21 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve kept your Advair and added ipratropium four times a day to help with any bronchospasm."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2156-07-21 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s helped. I’ll keep using it at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2156-07-21 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Also, you’ll take pantoprazole daily for stomach protection, and keep using lactulose and MiraLAX as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2156-07-21 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the lidocaine patch for my back pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2156-07-21 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, one patch daily. It’s safe to continue."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2156-07-21 10:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "My PCP is on vacation. Should I wait to follow up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2156-07-21 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Dr. Patel and Dr. Kim know about your stay. Call your PCP when they’re back, or sooner if you have issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2156-07-22 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re cleared to go home. Nurse will review all instructions with you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2156-07-22 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I feel much better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2156-07-22 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You did well. Remember: resume your insulin as before, keep feeds at 50 cc/hr, and call if pain or vomiting returns."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2156-07-22 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And no tramadol unless my doctor says so?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2156-07-22 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Use hydromorphone only if pain is severe. And follow up with your PCP in a week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2156-07-22 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Thanks for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2156-07-22 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. We’re discharging you to home with a clear mind and steady condition."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2156-07-13 16:55:00",
    "admission_end": "2156-07-22 13:45:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted with acute viral gastroenteritis causing severe diarrhea, vomiting, and abdominal pain, which exacerbated her chronic pancreatitis and gastroparesis. Over nine days, her symptoms resolved with conservative management including IV fluids, low-dose narcotics, and gradual resumption of tube feeds up to 50 cc/hr. Her type 1 diabetes was stabilized with adjusted insulin dosing, and psychiatric symptoms remained controlled on her baseline regimen. Stool studies ruled out bacterial pathogens. Pain management was transitioned from IV Dilaudid to oral hydromorphone for discharge, with tramadol discontinued due to patient refusal during admission. She was discharged home in stable condition with instructions to resume her prior insulin regimen, continue tube feeds, and follow up with her primary care provider.",
    "problems": [
      "Intestinal infection due to other organism, not elsewhere classified",
      "Chronic pancreatitis",
      "Diabetes with neurological manifestations, type I [juvenile type], uncontrolled",
      "Gastroparesis",
      "Abdominal pain, other specified site",
      "Asthma, unspecified type, unspecified",
      "Retention of urine, unspecified",
      "Borderline personality disorder",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Unspecified gastritis and gastroduodenitis, without mention of hemorrhage",
      "Iron deficiency anemia, unspecified"
    ]
  }
}
